    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0717" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg597"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Chargé to Acting Secretary of State
                        Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Adee</hi>: Acknowledging for Mr.
                    Takahira, receipt of your note of the 18th instant relative to the request of
                    the Russian Government, transmitted by the United States ambassador at St.
                    Petersburg to the effect that permission be given to Captain Ginter to replace
                    Captain Berlinski of the interned Russian transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lena</hi>, who is now in Russia on sick leave, I beg to state in reply that
                    the Japanese Government have no objection to such permission being granted by
                    the United States Government.</p>
                <p>The statement to the effect that Russian minister of marine has given assurance
                    that Captain Berlinski will take no part in the present war has been noted.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eki Hioki.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
